  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "What is the value in simplest form of the following expression?\n\n\\[ \\begin{aligned} &\\sqrt{1} + \\sqrt{1+3} + \\sqrt{1+3+5} \\\\ &\\quad {}+ \\sqrt{1+3+5+7} \\end{aligned} \\]",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(5\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(4 + \\sqrt{7} + \\sqrt{10}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(10\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(15\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(4 + 3\\sqrt{3} + 2\\sqrt{5} + \\sqrt{7}\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "c",
    "value": "10"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-12b-2020-p1.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The sum of the first \\(k\\) odd numbers equals \\(k^2,\\) so each radicand is a perfect square: \\[ \\begin{aligned} &\\sqrt{1} + \\sqrt{4} + \\sqrt{9} + \\sqrt{16} \\\\ &= 1 + 2 + 3 + 4 = 10. \\end{aligned} \\]\n\nThus, the correct answer is C.",
